title Mycelium Voucher r1 — a node's signed attestation binds a position to a named order-head
prompt baton prin recur — read REMEMBER + the 1,024-round itinerary + the six-season double-seat, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, approve own design rounds, send each finished increment as its own signed round, stop at custody gates.
think Read REMEMBER (git nib d405924bac; working tree clean, HEAD ff4b28d9ec folded the Statement arc), the 1,024-round itinerary, and the six-season double-seat expansion. The recent arc is Season D Mycelium — Cord · gossip · fact-batching · Knot · Tenure · Till · Purse · Pledge · Braid · Lapse · Statement, each a signed primitive, the Statement arc just closed (r1–r4). REMEMBER's frontier named a fresh Season D journey as next.
think Rather than pile another near-identical arc, I sought the genuine highest-Lindy crux the whole ledger set names but never fills. Read statement.rye and statement_bron.rye: the Statement reads a position and travels it byte-for-byte, yet a statement that travels is still only a READING — nothing binds those numbers to the real agreed order, so a holder could hand over any balance and the counterparty's only recourse would be to replay the whole ledger. The blind spot is proof of position without replay. That is Lindy (a ledger is only trustworthy to a stranger once a holder can prove standing without handing over the whole book) and crux-first (the hard-but-tractable move: bind a signed position to a single digest of the agreed order).
think Studied the seams: cord.commit (pub) yields one agreed order per arrival permutation; dag.hashes (pub) holds each block address; Sha256 is cord's hasher; kumara.sign/verify_bytes and Signature.toBytes/PublicKey.fromBytes are the signing surface (mirrored fold.rye's mint_fact). The order-head digest — a SHA-256 fold over the count and the ordered block addresses — is arrival-independent exactly because the committed order is. No cord edit needed: the order-head fold lives inside voucher.rye as its own bounded derivation.
think Named the journey the Voucher (comlink-tendency: clear/warm/safe, grep-clean — 0 hits — and fits the finance-noun subfamily Purse·Pledge·Till·Statement). Wrote the self-approved design read (active-designing/20260813-095216_…) naming the four-rung arc mirroring the seated shape: r1 crux · r2 travels (voucher_bron) · r3 across a Knot · r4 true to the bytes.
think Implemented r1 (mycelium/voucher.rye): order_head_of folds the committed order to one 32-byte digest; make_voucher reads an account's Statement out of ONE Dag and signs order-head · account · balance · reserved · received under a node key; verify_voucher checks the signature offline against the record's own node key; check_against(dag) re-derives the order-head and re-reads the Statement and confirms every signed field. Two contract asserts per function, positive // invariant: lines, explicit widths (pos_len 8 le u64, body_len fixed), copy_disjoint over memcpy.
obs GREEN on the first run across five scenes: open (Alice reserved 100), posted (reserve returns 0), lapsed (coins home, balance 100), arrival-independence inherited (a voucher made against one round-2 permutation checks against the other — the order-head folds to one digest, the Statement to one position), and tamper (flipped balance → BadSignature, wrong node key → BadSignature, an honest voucher for one ledger fails check_against a genuinely different — shorter — ledger). The rendered open voucher reads balance=0 reserved=100 received=100.
obs Additive discipline held: composed cord+fold+lapse+statement+kumara public API only, edited no module, each re-runs GREEN at the witness door. The order-head fold walks ≤ cord_max_blocks ordered hashes — bounded, no unbounded walk. TAME style check clean (voucher.rye not flagged), width-check exit 0. Demo node/keeper seeds — no key/funds/network/custody; a served voucher reaches the Comlink-served gate.
loom witness=mycelium_voucher_witness scenes=5 order_head_bytes=32 body_bytes=112 first_run=green
